<report>
<title>Woolf chi-square analysis of 2 by 2 series</title>
<block name="table">

<p><u>For table @table</u><br />
Percentages:  A = @{pc_a:roundu} C = @{pc_c:roundu} Total = @{pc_t:roundu}</p>
<block name="warn_small"><p><warn>WARNING: SMALL EXPECTED FREQUENCIES, CHECK BY EXACT METHODS</warn></p></block>
<p>Uncorrected Chi&#xb2; = @{table_chi_2:roundu} Chi = @{table_chi:roundu}<br />
Yates' corrected Chi&#xb2; = @{yates_chi_2:roundu} Chi = @{yates_chi:roundu} <pval>@{yates_chi_p:pval}</pval></p>

<block name="no_haldane">
<p><b>Without Haldane Correction:</b><br />
Odds ratio = @{odds:roundu}  log odds ratio = @{log:roundu}<br />
Variance of log odds ratio = @{var:roundu}  standard error = @{se:roundu}  weight = @{weight:roundu}<br />
Chi&#xb2; = @{chi_2:roundu} Chi = @{chi:roundu}<ci> </ci><pval>@{chi_p:pval}</pval><br />
<ci>Approximate @{pc:round2}% CI for log odds ratio = @{ci_from:roundu} to @{ci_to:roundu}</ci><br />
<ci>Giving an odds ratio of @{odds_from:roundu} to @{odds_to:roundu}</ci></p></block>
<block name="warn_no_haldane">
<p><warn>ODDS RATIO NOT COMPUTABLE WITHOUT HALDANE CORRECTION</warn></p>
</block>
<block name="haldane">

<p><b>With Haldane Correction:</b><br />
Odds ratio = @{odds:roundu}  log odds ratio = @{log:roundu}<br />
Variance of log odds ratio = @{var:roundu}  standard error = @{se:roundu}  weight = @{weight:roundu}<br />
Chi&#xb2; = @{chi_2:roundu}  Chi = @{chi:roundu} <pval>@{chi_p:pval}</pval><br />
<ci>Approximate @{pc:round2}% CI for log odds ratio = @{ci_from:roundu} to @{ci_to:roundu}</ci><br />
<ci>Giving an odds ratio of @{odds_from:roundu} to @{odds_to:roundu}</ci></p>
</block>
</block>
<br />
<block name="combined_no_haldane">
<p><b>For combined tables without Haldane correction:</b><br />
Number of Tables = @tables<br />
Mean log odds ratio = @{mean:roundu} giving odds ratio = @{odds:roundu}<br />
Variance of mean log odds ratio = @{var:roundu}  standard error = @{se:roundu}<br />
<ci>Approximate @{pc:round2}% CI for mean log odds ratio = @{ci_from:roundu} to @{ci_to:roundu}</ci><br />
<ci>Giving odds ratio of @{odds_from:roundu} to @{odds_to:roundu}</ci><br />
Chi&#xb2; for expected log odds ratio = 0 is @{chi_2:roundu} Chi = @{chi:roundu} <pval>@{chi_p:pval}</pval><br />
Chi&#xb2; for heterogeneity = @{het_chi_2:roundu} DF = @df <pval>@{het_chi_p:pval}</pval></p>
</block>
<block name="combined_with_haldane">

<p><b>For combined tables with Haldane correction:</b><br />
Number of tables = @tablesx<br />
Mean log odds ratio = @{meanx:roundu} giving odds ratio = @{oddsx:roundu}<br />
Variance of mean log odds ratio = @{varx:roundu}  standard error = @{sex:roundu}<br />
<ci>Approximate @{pc:round2}% CI for mean log odds ratio = @{ci_fromx:roundu} to @{ci_tox:roundu}</ci><br />
<ci>Giving odds ratio of @{odds_fromx:roundu} to @{odds_tox:roundu}</ci><br />
Chi&#xb2; for expected log odds ratio = 0 is @{chi_2x:roundu} Chi = @{chix:roundu} <pval>@{chi_px:pval}</pval><br />
Chi&#xb2; for heterogeneity = @{het_chi_2x:roundu} DF = @dfx <pval>@{het_chi_px:pval}</pval></p>
</block>
</report>
